# Grocery List - Production-Ready Cloud Sync Configuration
# To enable real-time cloud synchronization between multiple devices:
# 
# 1. Create a free Firebase project at: https://console.firebase.google.com/
# 2. Add a Web App: Project Settings -> General -> "Your apps" -> Add Web App (</>)
# 3. Enable Authentication:
#    - Go to Build -> Authentication -> Get started
#    - Under "Sign-in method", enable "Anonymous" (and optionally "Email/Password")
# 4. Enable Cloud Firestore:
#    - Go to Build -> Firestore Database -> Create database
#    - Choose a location close to you
#    - Copy & paste the contents of `firestore.rules` into the "Rules" tab in the Firebase console
# 5. Copy the configuration values below into your `.env` or `.env.local` file:

EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your_project_id.firebaseapp.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your_project_id
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your_project_id.appspot.com
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=your_messaging_sender_id
EXPO_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=your_app_id
